From: Maicon Alves <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:05:52 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 50/51] client: a picture of the world as it was left, for the
 handheld's world list

The handheld's world list, as Minecraft's Select World, shows a picture of each world. The client
takes it from the game's own frame: once the 3D view is drawn, before the hand, the HUD and the
menus, the middle square of the screen is scaled down to 64x64, as Minecraft's world icons, and
saved as icon.png in the world's folder.

It is taken when the pause menu opens, which is how a game is left from its menu, and on one more
frame that the loop draws when a signal ends the game: the handheld's START+SELECT sends SIGTERM.
Only a local game on a handheld (menu_handheld) takes it, and only when the 3D view goes straight to
the screen (no undersampling without post-processing): a 640x480 read and a PNG of about 6 KB each
time.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

